§1. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY / TRADEMARK / COPYRIGHT NON-AFFILIATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Software is an UNOFFICIAL, NON-COMMERCIAL fan tribute derivative work
inspired by the worldview publicly known as "Soul Land / 斗罗大陆" /
"Douluo Dalu", a series of novels and derivative media created by the
original author Tang Jia San Shao (hereinafter referred to as the
"Original Author") and associated publishers and rights holders
(collectively, the "Rights Holders").

(a) NO AFFILIATION. The Software is NOT affiliated with, sponsored by,
    endorsed by, authorized by, or in any way associated with the
    Original Author or any of the Rights Holders. No actual partnership,
    joint venture, employment, agency, or contractual relationship exists
    between the author of this Software ("Author") and any Rights Holder.

(b) TRADEMARK DISCLAIMER. All trademarks, service marks, trade names,
    logos, character names, place names, sect names, skill names, and
    similar identifiers that may appear in the Software's text data,
    configuration defaults, debug logs, or AI-generated content
    (collectively, "Marked Terms") are the property of their respective
    owners, including but not limited to the Original Author and the
    Rights Holders. The Author disclaims any proprietary interest in such
    Marked Terms. Use of these Marked Terms is for descriptive /
    referential purposes only (i.e., nominative fair use) and does not
    imply endorsement of or by the Rights Holders.

(c) NO ORIGINAL EXPRESSION REPRODUCED. The Software contains NO original
    prose, dialogue, plot, scenes, illustrations, photographs, audio
    recordings, or other expressive copyrightable content from the
    Original Work. All in-game content (spirit beasts, rings, skills,
    mechanisms, items, models, textures, language strings) is either:
       (1) Original code / art created by the Author and released under MIT;
       (2) Generated algorithmically by third-party AI services at runtime;
       (3) Common gameplay / cultural concepts (e.g., "ring of years",
           "soul skill") that exist in many works and the public domain.

(d) WORLDVIEW vs. EXPRESSION. The Software draws only upon the broadest,
    publicly-known "worldview" / "setting" elements (the so-called
    "ideas" / "scènes à faire" level), which by general legal consensus
    are not protected by copyright. No protectable "expression" is
    reproduced. Where Marked Terms appear in the Software, they refer to
    generic gameplay categories (e.g., a "spirit ring" item type) and
    not to any specific copyrighted scene, character, or storyline.

(e) DISCLAIMER OF ORIGINALITY. The Author makes no representation that
    the Software is an original work unrelated to the Original Work;
    it is, by its very nature, a derivative fan work, and is presented
    as such.

