§4. AI-GENERATED CONTENT DISCLAIMER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(a) GENERATIVE AI. The Software integrates with third-party generative
    AI services (currently DeepSeek / OpenAI-compatible APIs) to
    dynamically generate in-game content such as skill descriptions,
    primitive compositions, and parameter values at runtime.

(b) NO OWNERSHIP CLAIM. The Author does not claim authorship or
    ownership of any specific AI-generated output. Such output is
    governed by the terms of the respective AI service provider.

(c) CONTENT SAFETY. Although the Software includes an anomaly detector
    (SkillAnomalyDetector) that filters for forbidden keywords, numerical
    overflow, instant-kill patterns, and other abuse vectors, the
    Author does NOT warrant that AI-generated content is free of
    offensive, inappropriate, copyrighted-suggestive, or otherwise
    objectionable content.

(d) API KEY RESPONSIBILITY. The Author is not responsible for any
    charges, rate limits, account suspensions, or breaches of the AI
    provider's terms resulting from use of the Software. Users are
    responsible for their own API keys, usage, and compliance with
    the AI provider's terms of service.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§5. CLOUD SERVICE / NETWORK / DATA DISCLAIMER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(a) THIRD-PARTY CLOUD. The Software optionally syncs user-generated
    content (skill data) to a third-party cloud storage service
    (currently Aliyun OSS, https://www.aliyun.com/product/oss). This
    service is provided by Alibaba Cloud. The Author is not
    responsible for the availability, security, privacy, or terms of
    this third-party service.

(b) DATA COLLECTED. The Software transmits only:
       - anonymized uploader hash (cryptographic hash of player UUID);
       - in-game player name (as configured by the user);
       - skill data (name, description, execution steps) created by the
         user or generated by the AI on their behalf.
    The Software does NOT transmit: real names, email addresses,
    physical addresses, payment information, IP addresses (beyond what
    the underlying HTTP layer necessarily exposes to the cloud
    provider), or any other personally identifiable information beyond
    the in-game name.

(c) NO CENTRAL ACCOUNT. The Software does not require users to create
    an account with the Author. All data sent to the cloud is
    anonymous-by-design and tied only to a cryptographic hash.

(d) USER RESPONSIBILITY. Server administrators are responsible for:
       - informing their players of what data is transmitted;
       - obtaining any necessary consent under GDPR / CCPA / applicable
         privacy laws;
       - configuring the Software's cloud sync features in accordance
         with their jurisdiction's requirements.

(e) OFFLINE OPERATION. The Software is fully usable in "OFFLINE" mode
    (no cloud sync, no AI calls). All core gameplay functions work
    without any network connectivity.

